  "details": "The new right click to select player icon sounds good in theory, in practice it messes up a lot.\n\n- for one, I have the reticle off by default. Right click shows the reticle if I need it for precise pointing. So immediately I have to toggle the option off entirely.\n\n- two, it makes a very in the way visual every time. UI covering up precious screen space has been a recurring issue with recent VRChat updates.\n\n- three, it's too easy to accidently do.\n\nA lot of people don't realize, but VRChat already has an \"easy select\" method. Hold shift while you have your quick menu open. It doesn't get in the way, it's always been there if you need it, it's just not told to players. But if the right click to select is an absolute must add feature, there is an easy fix that at least doesn't cause as many issues.\n\n- Instead of right click to select, holding right click enables highlight, then left click.\n\n- Also probably have it off by default, the shift option is just so much less intrusive",
